---
import Header from '../components/Header.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';
---

<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="utf-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1" />
    <title>Docs — SigPi</title>
    <meta
      name="description"
      content="SigPi quick start: install, configure, and chat with your coding agent."
    />
    <link rel="icon" type="image/svg+xml" href="/favicon.svg" />
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="/styles/global.css" />
  </head>
  <body>
    <Header />

    <main class="docs">
      <h1>Quick start</h1>
      <p class="lead">
        From clone to your first conversation in about two minutes.
      </p>

      <h2>Requirements</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Node.js</strong> ≥ 22.19.0</li>
        <li><strong>pnpm</strong></li>
      </ul>

      <h2>1. Install</h2>
      <pre><code>git clone https://github.com/xiatianliang1024gm/sigpi
cd sigpi
pnpm install</code></pre>

      <h2>2. Configure</h2>
      <p>
        Run <code>pnpm dev init</code>, then edit
        <code>~/.sigpi/config.toml</code> with your API key and model.
      </p>
      <pre><code>[models.default]
base_url = "https://api.openai.com/v1"
api_key  = "sk-..."
name     = "gpt-4o"</code></pre>
      <p>
        SigPi works with any provider that speaks the OpenAI chat completions API —
        OpenAI, Anthropic via proxy, Ollama, LiteLLM, and more. Overrides:
        <code>.sigpi/config.toml</code> in your project, or environment variables.
      </p>

      <h2>3. Chat</h2>
      <pre><code>pnpm dev chat</code></pre>
      <p>
        That's it. You're talking to an agent that can see your code.
      </p>

      <h2>Resume a session</h2>
      <pre><code>pnpm dev chat --session &lt;id&gt;</code></pre>

      <h2>Useful commands</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><code>pnpm dev session new --title "fix login bug"</code></li>
        <li><code>pnpm dev session list</code></li>
        <li>Inside chat: <code>/summary</code>, <code>/compact</code>, <code>/resume</code>, <code>/model</code></li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Skills</h2>
      <p>
        Drop a <code>SKILL.md</code> into <code>.sigpi/skills/</code> — the agent
        loads it automatically. Follows the
        <a href="https://agentskills.io/specification">Agent Skills spec</a>.
      </p>
    </main>

    <Footer />
  </body>
</html>
